INSTALL — CUDA Parallel Merge Sort capstone
===========================================

Prerequisites
-------------
- An NVIDIA GPU with the CUDA Toolkit (>= 11.0). The Coursera course lab
  already provides this at /usr/local/cuda.
- A C++14 host compiler (g++), which the CUDA Toolkit uses via nvcc.

There are no third-party library dependencies: the program uses only the CUDA
runtime and the C++ standard library.

Build (Linux / Coursera lab)
----------------------------
From the repository root:

    make

If nvcc is not on the default path, point the Makefile at it:

    make NVCC=/usr/local/cuda/bin/nvcc CUDA_PATH=/usr/local/cuda

Run everything (build, sort, benchmark, log)
--------------------------------------------
    ./run.sh

This produces, under proof/:
    run_log.txt          full console log
    benchmark.csv        GPU vs CPU timing across input sizes
    sample_input.csv     small readable input array
    sample_sorted.csv    its sorted output
    input_<N>.csv        the large input array (git-ignored)
    sorted_<N>.csv       the large sorted output (git-ignored)

Manual usage
------------
    ./bin/cuda_merge_sort --size 1048576 --output sorted.csv
    ./bin/cuda_merge_sort --input my_array.csv --output sorted.csv
    ./bin/cuda_merge_sort --benchmark --bench-out proof/benchmark.csv
    ./bin/cuda_merge_sort --help

Cleaning
--------
    make clean
